  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). The statement 'Taxes' 4,613,909 is split using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2): Property 3,991,620 + Motor Vehicle 552,515 + Lodging tax 69,774 = 4,613,909 exactly; inheritance tax is its own line. Sale of assets 22,194 is printed under Other Financing Sources and recorded as other_financing. Beginning/ending fund balances from p4; beginning cash is not printed (null); ending cash = Cash + Restricted cash on p3 (printed Total Assets). Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Assets and Fund Balances (p3), whose totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund column from the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (pp8-9; budget-basis Local 1,148,950 includes sale of assets 4,508, combining column shows 1,144,442); the other General Fund sub-funds (Inheritance Tax, Self-Health Insurance, Veterans Aid, Noxious Weed) from the combining statement p5; Road Fund and American Rescue Plan Fund from their budget schedules (pp10-11); nonmajor funds per fund column from the combining statement pp6-7 (Drug Law Enforcement Fund had no activity). General Fund, library and courthouse 'Taxes' lines in detail stay unlabeled (no exact printed breakdown per fund); Visitors Promotion/Improvement taxes are lodging tax (fund name, tie to the printed Lodging tax 69,774). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
